    {
      "number": 598,
      "url": "https://github.com/pirate-social-club/api-next/pull/598",
      "title": "Implement account-free Study practice and durable guest recovery",
      "state": "open",
      "draft": false,
      "merged": false,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-13T05:55:30Z",
      "head": "efe07c5acda838041b3e47a6ef7f1a48ea9b16d3",
      "base": "4a791f27fb7c983689fe75150953be67ed25f709",
      "changed_files": 247,
      "body": "Adds account-free prepared Study practice with durable browser ownership, server-scored spoken answers, saved-result recovery, retention and proof-authorized audio deletion. The Worker requires explicit nonproduction composition and concrete native readiness for four distinct restricted PostgreSQL roles. Current limits and disclosure gate new provider work; accepted checkpoints recover the original resource and provider result without redispatch.\n\nSixteen learning declarations are source-admitted. Five accounting declarations and reward-capable mode remain unavailable. Source migrations 0248\u20130263 and the regenerated baseline/reset preserve ordinary Account/Karaoke ownership. Immutable client 0.118.0 preserves all historical releases and operation wire shapes. New restricted Telegram learner accounts now receive their immutable owner in the same birth transaction, before Study; existing learners and recovery never provision one late.\n\nValidation:\n- Four native readiness cases and three canonical default Worker/native/HNS journeys pass. Provider/storage/host boundaries are local fixtures.\n- Native public preparedness/private Study journey: nine cases pass, covering original COMMIT recovery, saved-checkpoint replay and late audio/deletion reconciliation. Five native authority cases also pass.\n- Actual ordinary Study/reward compatibility: five cases pass. A later seven-file run passes 25 of 26 cases, including Study concurrency/lifecycle, current Karaoke policy/persona/leaderboard, exact Telegram inline/queue and historical reset. Its remaining owned-baseline ACL assertion is corrected; the genuine learner successor passes 85 assertions, including denied-birth rollback and grant/revoke continuity.\n- Full maintained check and test pass at ae602637: 5,996 unit cases, 24 SQLite/DO cases, 22 Node cases and all 242 Workerd cases; three existing environment skips. Both required fresh FFmpeg completion markers are verified. Frozen historical regression adapters verify their exact release119 and PR592 schema/runtime boundaries; current cases retain the current implementation.\n- Final candidate efe07c5 differs only by the reviewed owned learner ACL fixture correction. Its genuine native learner case passes 85 assertions, and its fresh full maintained check/test passes all the counts above with both required media markers. Owned application/PostgreSQL containers are physically removed and source stays clean. Hosted CI38353040821 matches that exact published head; canonical acceptance awaits the remaining required hosted checks.\n\nProduction remains paused. This PR does not apply live migrations, provision managed roles, deploy, activate features or perform funded operations. After protected canonical acceptance, the frozen learning/client custody handoff permits accounting serially and guest UI under the agreed contract. Shared financial scheduler composition, live adapters and composed staging recovery remain separate acceptance work.\n"
    },
    {
      "number": 597,
      "url": "https://github.com/pirate-social-club/api-next/pull/597",
      "title": "fix(jobs): bound recovery alert scans and preserve failure signals",
      "state": "open",
      "draft": true,
      "merged": false,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-13T06:00:16Z",
      "head": "6fb1014ba3679fb8452daaf493d2da2a6f3c4af6",
      "base": "4a791f27fb7c983689fe75150953be67ed25f709",
      "changed_files": 15,
      "body": "**Blocked on shared migration allocation with [#598](https://github.com/pirate-social-club/api-next/pull/598). Do not merge this PR or apply its cursor migration yet.** #598 currently uses 0248\u20130263. The proposal is to keep those numbers, use #597's prepared `0264_media_alignment_alert_cursor.sql`, and land #598 first, subject to the cloud/schema owner's approval. After #598 lands, rebase this PR and regenerate the combined baseline/reset before release.\n\nSpaces verification failures emit duplicate warnings, and the media sweep repeatedly logs stored terminal recovery failures as errors. Those failures need deduplicated high-severity alert coverage, with bounded observation work in the shared scheduled handler.\n\nThe verifier suppresses only warnings already emitted by the adapter, preserving job warnings for pre-request rejection, unlogged exceptions, outer timeouts, and interruptions. The media logger downgrades only a returned stored terminal diagnostic; fresh Workflow lookup and storage failures remain errors.\n\nThe alert query for retained errors includes the sweep's shared eligibility plus historical published recovery actions. Each run inspects at most 50 Workflow candidates using a separate `media-alignment-alerts` row in `recovery_inspection_cursors`, advances the two-part key under `FOR UPDATE`, and wraps at the end. The transaction commits before Workflow I/O. Healthy candidates, malformed candidate payloads, and failed observations advance the cursor, so later candidates get a turn without scanning the whole pipeline every minute. Cursor, query, and storage failures still emit an error.\n\nThe cursor migration is held pending the allocation and dependency resolution described above. It seeds only the new cursor; existing media and DATA sweep cursors remain independent. Generated PostgreSQL baseline and reset seeds are updated. The instrumental policy migration test now stops at its target migration rather than assuming it is the latest.\n\nValidation before renumbering, on 2071aea3: all CI checks passed, including full application tests and Worker dry runs, every PostgreSQL 17 partition and aggregate gate, PostgreSQL 18 compatibility, HNS, secret-boundary, and dependency audit. Local `bun run check`, 54 affected unit tests, the PostgreSQL no-recovery-action regression, and all three instrumental policy PostgreSQL tests passed. The paging regression inspects 50/1/50/1 candidates over four runs, with alert suppression. PostgreSQL verifies committed cursor progress before Workflow I/O, wrapping, deduplication, and an unchanged media sweep cursor.\n\nLocal broad runs had two unchanged staging-release unit timeouts, both passing in isolation, and two unchanged Self SDK runtime timeouts at the default 5 seconds, both passing with a 30-second CLI budget. All other local Node and Worker runtime suites passed. CI passed the full suite with the repository's default timeouts.\n\nThe live Spaces origin failure and stranded media submission still require verifier-host and staging PostgreSQL access, which are not configured in this environment.\n\n\nRenumbering candidate `6fb1014b`: the cursor SQL is unchanged and its SHA-256 is unchanged. `checksums.json` now names `0264`; baseline and reset files were regenerated and remain byte-identical on the current main base. Compared with #598 at `efe07c5`, the prospective combined inventory has 264 checksum-verified migrations with unique ordinals 0001\u20130264 and 247 unchanged shared migrations. The 27 existing migration/ledger guard tests pass. Fresh local checks and hosted CI are running. These branch-local checks do not establish acceptance of the combined implementation; after #598 lands, this PR still requires rebase, combined regeneration and fresh checks."
    }
  ],
